From ff1b3b04ca389b220d63d2f47d01194375feddd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:10:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] serve: STRATA_PARK_ASYNC=1 captures a finished
 request's conversation beside the slots

With the conversation cache on, every request that does not continue the
live session parks it first, and the capture (the running state, the
checkpoints and the K/V of every stage, ~65-150 ms on a 4-card split) ran
at the next request's start with every pipelined slot group drained.

STRATA_PARK_ASYNC=1 (default off) starts that capture right after the
request (its DONE / BADM), on one persistent thread per stage device,
while the slots decode.  Nothing writes the main sessions until the next
request, so it is the image the park there would take; the next request
only decides: park it (superseded copies, budget, RAM floor and put, in
the park's order) or, when it continues the live session, stop it and
keep a complete capture's K/V pages for the next park, as after a
restore.  The capture copies through two pinned 16 MiB staging blocks per
device on the thread's private stream, with no device-wide wait (the
devices are synchronized once when it starts, before any group runs),
and can be stopped between blocks.  Its RAM admission does not evict;
what does not fit is left to the synchronous park.  #879's flush, VRAM
and SAVE/RESTORE stop and drop it; the elastic K/V and groups running
past a request (STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP) keep the synchronous park.  With the
switch, retained K/V pages are also dropped before a slot's give-back
overwrites the main session.

STRATA_PARK_THREADS=1 (implied by the above) captures a layer split's
stage images at once in the synchronous park.  STRATA_PARK_ASYNC_VERIFY=1
also takes the synchronous capture at every park and stops the engine if
a byte differs.

Core: ConversationCapture (device_sync, staging, cancel) overloads of
conversation_kv_save, conversation_checkpoint_save and
conversation_snapshot_save; the existing signatures copy as before.
conversation_checkpoints_stage_copy (split's per-stage list, copied),
conversation_image_same, ConversationCache::restore_reuse / budget.
Tests: staged, unstaged-stoppable, cancelled and retained-page captures
equal the plain one (conversation_snapshot_test); stage copy == split,
deep compare, restore_reuse (conversation_cache_test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
